//! The `stroke` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines the color
//! or SVG paint server used to draw an element's stroke. As such, `stroke` only has an effect on
//! elements that can be given a stroke (for example, `rect` or `ellipse`); see the page on the SVG
//! `stroke` attribute for a complete list. When declared, the CSS value overrides any value of the
//! element's `stroke` SVG attribute.
//!
//! Initial: stroke-dasharray: none; stroke-dashoffset: 0; stroke-linecap: butt; stroke-linejoin:
//! miter; stroke-miterlimit: 4; stroke-opacity: 1; stroke-width: 1px. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: No paint is applied in this layer.
//!
//! Grammar: <paint>
//!
//! Specification: https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/painting.html#StrokeProperty
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/stroke
